/E (India's ambition to emerge as a global scientific powerhouse is facing a credibility challenge after recording the world's second-highest number of research paper retractions in 2025, raising concerns over research integrity and academic standards.While the country contributes around 5 per cent of global research publications, it accounts for 21 per cent of all paper retractions worldwide, highlighting what experts describe as a systemic problem rather than isolated instances of error.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [16]
>>
